1: OpenBLAS packages

Installation from OpenBLAS Source 
Download from project homepage. http://xianyi.github.com/OpenBLAS/
Or, check out codes from git://github.com/xianyi/OpenBLAS.git



2: How to making an SDPA binary

cd GENERAL
git clone https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS.git
cd OpenBLAS
make clean
make CC=gcc FC=gfortran USE_OPENMP=1 INTERFACE64=1
cd ..
make distclean
export CC=gcc
export CXX=g++
export F77=gfortran
export CFLAGS="-funroll-all-loops -O2 -fopenmp -DINTSIZE64 -DDIMACS_PRINT"
export CXXFLAGS="-funroll-all-loops -O2 -fopenmp -DINTSIZE64 -DDIMACS_PRINT"
export FFLAGS="-funroll-all-loops -O2 -fopenmp -fdefault-integer-8 -fallow-argument-mismatch"
./configure --with-blas="-L./lib -lopenblas -lgomp" --with-lapack="-L./lib -lopenblas -lgomp"
make -j $(nproc)


2b: Known issues on macOS / Apple Silicon (Homebrew GCC + SDKROOT)

On macOS (verified on an Apple Silicon Mac running macOS 26 with
Xcode, no standalone Command Line Tools package installed), CC=gcc /
FC=gfortran above must point at a real GNU toolchain, not Apple's
clang aliased as "gcc" -- Apple clang does not support -fopenmp or
-fdefault-integer-8, and this project needs both. Install one with
Homebrew and use its versioned binaries:

    brew install gcc
    # use gcc-15/g++-15/gfortran-15 (or whatever version brew installs)
    # in place of gcc/g++/gfortran below.

With that alone, both the OpenBLAS build and SDPA's own ./configure
step fail with an error like:

    fatal error: _bounds.h: No such file or directory

This is because Homebrew's gcc bottle is built with a hardcoded
--with-sysroot pointing at a specific "/Library/Developer/
CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSXNN.sdk" version. On a machine where only
Xcode.app is installed (no separate Command Line Tools package), that
exact path does not exist, gcc silently drops it, and the compiler is
left with no system include path at all. Work around it by exporting
SDKROOT so gcc/gfortran pick up the SDK Xcode actually provides:

    export SDKROOT="$(xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path)"

Export this before building OpenBLAS and before running SDPA's own
./configure and make. No source changes are needed once SDKROOT is
set; this is purely a local toolchain/environment fix. (See the
sibling sdpa-gmp and sdpa-dd repositories for other, unrelated macOS
build issues found in their vendored external/ sources.)


3: How to execute an SDPA binary

export OMP_NUM_THREADS=??? (# of threads for SDPA and BLAS Library)

For example,
export OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 (If your computer has 8 CPU cores.)

./sdpa intputfile outputfile



 

